      "id": 486874,
      "username": "francis1",
      "name": "francis1",
      "created_at": "2025-11-19T07:40:14.933Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I’m a big fan of ERPNext and am excited about its future. To help it compete with larger, well-funded proprietary systems, I was wondering if the community has discussed alternative funding models.</p>\n<p>Perhaps introducing an official “Enterprise Edition” with advanced features or bundled support could provide Frappe with the stable resources needed for:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>More aggressive marketing to increase brand awareness.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Expanding the core development team to speed up the roadmap.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Investing in high-quality documentation and training materials.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The goal would be to strengthen the project without compromising the open-source values we all appreciate. A rising tide lifts all boats, and a more successful ERPNext project would create more opportunities for everyone in our community.</p>\n<p>I’m curious to hear what others think about this</p>",
